<p><a name=3D"keyword-structure-and-definitions"></a></p>
<h2 id=3D"keyword-structure-and-definitions">Keyword Structure and Definiti=
ons</h2>
<p><a name=3D"keyword-collection"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"keyword-collection">Keyword Collection</h3>
<p>Keyword values stored on the document can be accessed through a GET on t=
he <code>/documents/{documentId}/keywords</code> endpoint.  This response c=
ontains the following:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>items</td>
<td>An array of keywords grouped by the keyword group they belong to.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>keywordGuid</td>
<td>Global unique identifier that ensures integrity of restricted keyword v=
alues.  This value must be passed back during keyword modification.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><a name=3D"keyword-groups"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"keyword-groups">Keyword Groups</h3>
<p>Keywords that belong to a given document are grouped together into Keywo=
rd Groups which are used to classify and logically group the Keywords. When=
 a developer needs to access these Keywords, they will be interacting with =
one of three <a href=3D"https://sdk.onbase.com/rest/OnBase/Foundation26.1/d=
ocument/programmers-guide/working-with-keywords.html#keyword-group-storage-=
types">Keyword Group Storage Types</a>, each of which has a distinct purpos=
e within the object model.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>keywords</td>
<td>An array of keywords in the group.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>typeGroupId</td>
<td>The keyword type group identifier. This field will be omitted when not =
associated with a SingleInstance or MultiInstance type group.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>groupId</td>
<td>The identifier for the instance of the keyword group of Multi-Instance =
Keyword Group. This value is stored in the database and is created when the=
 document is stored or saved.  This field will be omitted when not associat=
ed with a MultiInstance type group or a new instance is being created.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>instanceId</td>
<td>The identifier assigned by the server for the instance of the keyword g=
roup of Multi-Instance Keyword Group and used for tracking restricted keywo=
rds. This field will be omitted when not associated with a MultiInstance ty=
pe group or a new instance is being created.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><a name=3D"keyword-group-storage-types"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"keyword-group-storage-types">Keyword Group Storage Types</h4>
<p><a name=3D"standalone-keyword-group"></a></p>
<h5 id=3D"standalone-keyword-group">Standalone Keyword Group</h5>
<p>Standalone Keywords are a grouped collection of keywords whose keyword t=
ype does not belong to a Single-Instance or Multi-Instance Group Type.  Thi=
s Keyword Group type can be determined by the absence of a set groupId and =
typeGroupId properties.  Keywords within this group type are allowed to hav=
e multiple instances of the same type as long as they have unique values (T=
his does not apply to any other Keyword Group).  These keywords may appear =
split into multiple keyword groups which reflects the order that they are c=
onfigured to appear on the document type.</p>
<p><a name=3D"single-instance-keyword-group"></a></p>
<h5 id=3D"single-instance-keyword-group">Single-Instance Keyword Group</h5>
<p>Keyword Types that belong to the Keyword Type Group may only be assigned=
 one value. In other words, a given Keyword Type Group may only contain a s=
ingle instance of the Keywords within the group. If the Keyword Type Group =
is then configured such that it does not allow multiple instances of the Ke=
yword Type Group, it is referred to as a Single-Instance Keyword Group.</p>
<p>Each Single-Instance Keyword Group contains a list of all Keywords assig=
ned to the document that are part of that same Keyword Type Group. These gr=
oups will have a property typeGroupId set corresponding to it's Keyword Typ=
e Group Id and groupId will be absent.</p>
<p><a name=3D"multi-instance-keyword-group"></a></p>
<h5 id=3D"multi-instance-keyword-group">Multi-Instance Keyword Group</h5>
<p>Multi-Instance Keyword Type Groups are simply Keyword Type Groups that c=
an have multiple instances of the group on a document. These groups can be =
identified by having both the groupId, which corresponds to the instance Id=
, and typeGroupId set.</p>
<p><a name=3D"configuration-data"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"configuration-data">Configuration Data</h3>
<p>Keyword values and the configuration data in this API are separate. To c=
orrectly present keyword values, a call to retrieve the Keyword Type inform=
ation for the document must be performed. The calls needed to retrieve all =
the required information are:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><code>GET: /documents/{documentId}</code>,
<code>GET: /document-types/{documentTypeId}/keyword-type-groups</code>,
<code>GET: /keyword-type-groups</code> with an optional list of id or syste=
mName properties, and
<code>GET: /keyword-types</code> with an optional list of id or systemName =
properties</p>
</blockquote>
<p><a name=3D"keyword-options"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"keyword-options">Keyword Options</h4>
<p>Keyword Options property is embedded in the <code>GET: /document-types/{=
documentTypeId}/keyword-type-groups</code> endpoint and contains the follow=
ing properties:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>requiredForArchivalKeywordTypeIds</td>
<td>List of Ids of Keyword Types that need to be added to a Document with a=
 value to be stored.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>requiredForRetrievalKeywordTypeIds</td>
<td>List of Ids of Keyword Types that are needed to perform a Document Retr=
ieval.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>readOnlyKeywordTypeIds</td>
<td>List of Ids of Keyword Types that are for display only and cannot be ed=
ited by the User on the configured Document Type.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><a name=3D"retrieving-keywords"></a></p>
<h2 id=3D"retrieving-keywords">Retrieving Keywords</h2>
<p>Keywords values can be directly retrieved on a document with a GET reque=
st on <code>/documents/{documentId}/keywords</code>, but this request only =
gives you some of the data to display Keywords to a user.  This section des=
cribes all the calls that are needed in order to retrieve all of the <a hre=
f=3D"https://sdk.onbase.com/rest/OnBase/Foundation26.1/document/programmers=
-guide/working-with-keywords.html#configuration-data">Configuration Data</a=
> with the starting point of having the Document Id.</p>
<p><a name=3D"retrieving-keyword-type-information"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"retrieving-keyword-type-information">Retrieving Keyword Type Info=
rmation</h3>
<p><a name=3D"get-keyword-type-information-for-document-type"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"get-keyword-type-information-for-document-type">Get Keyword Type =
Information For Document Type</h4>
<p>A GET request on <code>/documents/{documentId}</code> is needed to retri=
eve the Document Type Id so that a GET request on <code>/document-types/{do=
cumentTypeId}/keyword-type-groups</code> can be used to retrieve the list o=
f Keyword Type Ids, Keyword Type Group Ids, and <a href=3D"https://sdk.onba=
se.com/rest/OnBase/Foundation26.1/document/programmers-guide/working-with-k=
eywords.html#keyword-options">Keyword Options</a>.</p>
<p><strong><em>Example</em></strong></p>
<p>Retrieving Document Type Id from Document with Id of <strong><em>'123'</=
em></strong></p>
