<h3 id=3D"retrieving-keyword-values">Retrieving Keyword Values</h3>
<p>A request to GET on <code>/documents/{documentId}/keywords</code> return=
s a property <code>items</code>, which contains the list of Keyword values =
and Keyword Type Id, and Keyword GUID, which will be needed for updating Ke=
yword Values.</p>
<p>Keyword Types can be configured with the <code>isSecurityMasked</code> p=
roperty (see <a href=3D"https://sdk.onbase.com/rest/OnBase/Foundation26.1/d=
ocument/programmers-guide/working-with-keywords.html#get-all-keyword-type-i=
nformation-for-keyword-types-on-document">Get All Keyword Type Information =
for Keyword Types On Document</a>). Whether the actual Keyword Value or a m=
asked placeholder is returned for these Keyword Types depends on the <code>=
unmask</code> query string parameter and the requesting user's rights:</p>
<ul class=3D"list">
<li>If <code>unmask</code> is <strong>not</strong> sent, or is sent as <cod=
e>false</code>, security masked Keyword Values will always be returned mask=
ed, regardless of the user's access rights.</li>
<li>If <code>unmask</code> is sent as <code>true</code> and the user <stron=
g>has</strong> the Security Masked Keywords access right, the <code>value</=
code> and <code>formattedValue</code> properties will contain the actual, u=
nmasked Keyword Value.</li>
<li>If <code>unmask</code> is sent as <code>true</code> and the user <stron=
g>does not have</strong> the Security Masked Keywords access right, the <co=
de>value</code> and <code>formattedValue</code> properties will still be re=
turned masked.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong><em>Example</em></strong></p>
