<p><a name=3D"updating-keywords"></a></p>
<h2 id=3D"updating-keywords">Updating Keywords</h2>
<p>The endpoint used to do Keyword modification is a PUT on <code>/document=
s/{documentId}/keywords</code>.  Keyword Modification is only supported by =
passing the entire collection of Keywords into this request.  Therefore any=
 Keyword Objects or Keyword Groups not included in the request will result =
in their deletion.  For example a request with only one Keyword Object with=
 a Document with multiple Keywords attached to the <code>items</code> objec=
t will result in a Document with only that one Keyword Value or a Request w=
ith an empty <code>items</code> object will delete all Keywords.</p>
<p><a name=3D"update-keywords-request-body"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"update-keywords-request-body">Update Keywords Request Body</h3>
<p><a name=3D"keyword-guid-request-property"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"keyword-guid-request-property">Keyword Guid Request Property</h4>
<p> The Keyword Guid property is used to ensure that the consumer does not =
edit Restricted Keyword Values. This value is provided by a GET on <code>/d=
ocuments/{documentId}/keywords</code>.  This property must be included even=
 if there are no restricted keywords, and failure to do so will result in a=
n Error Response. This property also changes after every update, so for eve=
ry new keyword update you must perform a GET, and then take the keywordGuid=
 from that GET and include it in the PUT request for the new keyword update=
.</p>
<p><a name=3D"items-request-property"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"items-request-property">Items Request Property</h4>
<p> This property is also the same as a GET on <code>/documents/{documentId=
}/keywords</code> and if the response body of that request was used as the =
request body, this request would work with no changes being made.  This col=
lection must be the full list of Keywords to be stored on the Document, not=
 just the changes.  If an empty list is sent, all the Keywords will be remo=
ved from the Document.</p>
<p><a name=3D"keyword-operations"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"keyword-operations">Keyword Operations</h3>
<p><strong><em>Prior to making any changes to a given Keyword Value, the <a=
 href=3D"https://sdk.onbase.com/rest/OnBase/Foundation26.1/document/program=
mers-guide/working-with-keywords.html#keyword-options">Keyword Options</a> =
should be checked to ensure that the Keyword Type whose value is being modi=
fied is not marked Read Only for the Document Type.  Updating a Keyword tha=
t is Read Only will result in a 400 Bad Request.</em></strong></p>
<p>All the following actions are made by manipulating the response form a G=
ET on <code>/documents/{documentId}/keywords</code> request followed by a P=
UT on <code>/documents/{documentId}/keywords</code> with result attached as=
 the request body.</p>
<p><a name=3D"edit-a-keyword-value"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"edit-a-keyword-value">Edit a Keyword Value</h4>
<p>To modify a Keyword Value, the value property off of the Keyword object =
for the matching Keyword Type needs to be modified.</p>
<p>If the Keyword Type being modified has <code>isSecurityMasked</code> set=
, the requesting user must have the Security Masked Keywords access right t=
o update its value. If the user has this access right, the update will be p=
rocessed normally. If the user does not have this access right, the request=
 will fail with a <code>403 Forbidden</code> response and no Keywords on th=
e Document will be updated.</p>
<p><strong><em>Example</em></strong></p>
<p>Modifying Keyword with type Id of <strong><em>'1'</em></strong> from <st=
