<h2 id=3D"expanding-autofill-keyword-sets">Expanding AutoFill Keyword Sets<=
/h2>
<p>OnBase has the concept of "AutoFill Keyword Sets" (AFKS). These are grou=
ps of related Keyword values that can be automatically filled in when given=
 a value for a primary Keyword. An example is a group of Keywords that repr=
esent employee information, like Employee ID, First Name, Last Name, and Ti=
tle. In this example, inputting a valid Employee ID will lead to the other =
Keywords being filled in with the correct first name, last name, and title.=
 During archival and reindexing in clients with a graphical user interface,=
 like the Unity Client, AutoFill Keyword Sets are expanded after inputting =
a value for the primary keyword and tabbing away. The Document Management A=
PI offers similar functionality for expansion through the <code>/indexing-m=
odifiers</code> endpoint. The flow for expansion can be complicated dependi=
ng on the configuration settings of the Autofill Keyword Set and whether th=
ere are multiple matches for the primary Keyword value in the AutoFill Keyw=
ord.</p>
<p><a name=3D"afks-expansion-flow"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"expansion-flow">Expansion Flow</h3>
<p>The diagram below shows the flow for AutoFill Keyword Set expansion.</p>
<p class=3D"img-container"><img src=3D"https://sdk.onbase.com/rest/OnBase/F=
oundation26.1/document/programmers-guide/images/afks-expansion-flow.png" al=
t=3D"AutoFill Keyword Set Expansion"></p>
<p>A consumer sends a POST request to <code>/indexing-modifers</code>. Afte=
r the request is sent, the following behaviors are executed corresponding t=
o the configuration of the AFKS:</p>
<p><strong>Expand All Matches</strong> - If the configuration of the AFKS i=
s set to "Expand All Matching Instances," then all AutoFill Keyword Set Dat=
a Sets matching the given primary Keyword value will be expanded and a <cod=
e>200 Ok</code> response will be returned with the expanded AFKS in the <co=
de>keywordCollection</code> property of the response.</p>
<p>The rest of the behaviors are for AFKS where "Expand All Matching Instan=
ces" is not set. If the AutoFill Keyword Set is not configured to "Expand A=
ll Matching Instances" and there is only one matching Data Set, then that m=
atching Data Set will be expanded and sent back in the <code>keywordCollect=
ion</code>. If there are multiple matching Data Sets, one of the following =
flows will be triggered, depending on the settings of the AutoFill Keyword =
Set.</p>
<p><strong>Multiple Selection</strong> - If there are multiple matching Aut=
oFill Keyword Set Data Sets for the given primary Keyword value, the respon=
se will be a <code>300 Multiple Choice</code> and contain the matching Data=
 Sets, i.e. the Keyword values for all Keywords in the set, for all the mat=
ches. The consumer will then choose which of these to expand. The response =
will also include a property called <code>selectMultiple</code>. If "Allow =
Multiple AutoFill Keyword Set Selection" is checked in the configuration se=
ttings of the AFKS, then <code>selectMultiple</code> will be true and the c=
onsumer will be able to choose multiple Data Sets to expand. The consumer w=
ill then send a new POST request to <code>/indexing-modifiers</code> with t=
he desired AFKS Data Set IDs included in the <code>autoFillKeywordSetDataId=
s</code> property. The expanded AFKS(s) will be returned in the <code>keywo=
rdCollection</code> of the response.</p>
<p><strong>Single Selection</strong> - Begins like "Multiple Selection" but=
 "Allow Multiple AutoFill Keyword Set Selection" is <em>not</em> checked fo=
r the AFKS. Thus <code>selectMultiple</code> in the <code>300 Multiple Choi=
ce</code> response will be false. The consumer will then send a new POST re=
quest to <code>/indexing-modifiers</code> with the AFKS Data Set ID of the =
one Data Set they wish exapnded included in the <code>autoFillKeywordSetDat=
aIds</code> property. The expanded AFKS will be returned in the <code>keywo=
rdCollection</code> of the response. If more than one Data Set ID is sent i=
n the request, an error will be returned.</p>
<p><a name=3D"afks-expansion-examples"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"examples">Examples</h3>
